The 1946NEL_Playoffs.EBA file includes all games from the 1946 New England League playoffs, including the Nashua Dodgers team featuring Roy Campanella and Don Newcombe.
The 1946NEL.EBA file is currently empty but will contain regular season games from the 1946 New England League playoffs.

All of these files are licensed by a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0) license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

While the bp_generate_box.py script can be used to generate text-based box scores similar to the format used by Retrosheet, an HTML format provides more information and flexibility, especially if a full season of games for a league is contained in an .EBA file.

1. Sources of truth:

a) Excel file "1946 New England League.xlsx" (not checked into this folder) is the source of truth for the regular season schedule and results. 
   For the 1946 New England League this file is reasonably complete, though some game times are missing and additional details are likely to be found as I fill in the gaps in my box score inventory.

b) The 1946NEL.EBA (currently empty) and 1946NEL_Playoffs.EBA files are the source of the truth for the BOX SCORES and this data is read in first by bp_generate_box_html.py BEFORE reading in the schedule files that are derives from the Excel file (see below). 
   The assumption is that 1946NEL.EBA will contain regular season games in chronological order. 
   The 1946NEL_Playoffs.EBA file contains playoff games organized by SERIES and then chronologically.

c) The 1946NEL_playoffs_config.txt file was created manually to be in sync with the .EBA file data for the playoff games. The goal is to provide context for each playoff series.


2. Use Excel to export the Schedule tab of "1946 New England League.xlsx" as "1946 New England League from Excel.csv". An example of this is in this folder.

3. Use bp_generate_schedule_files_from_csv.py to generate 1946_actual_schedule.csv and 1946_original_schedule.csv files (the Try2 copies are currently the latest). Examples are in this folder.

4. For regular season output, do the following:

bp_generate_box_html.py 1946NEL.EBA 1946NEL_RegularSeason.htm -a 1946_actual_schedule_Try2.csv -o 1946_original_schedule_Try2.csv


5. For playoffs output, do the following:

bp_generate_box_html.py 1946NEL_Playoffs.EBA 1946NEL_Playoffs.htm -p 1946NEL_playoffs_config.txt


The HTML style sheet is based on David Waldron's daily box score page (https://www.waldrn.com/boxscores/) but I modified it to suit a multiple day format. 
This allows an entire season (regular season or playoffs) can be viewed in a single file.
